{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And they turned from there.</b> From the place where Abraham escorted them." "<b>And Abraham was still standing before YHWH.</b> But he did not go to stand before Him — rather, the Holy One, blessed be He, came to him and said to him, ״the outcry of Sodom and Gomorrah, for it is great.״ So should it not have been written, ״and YHWH was still standing over Abraham״? Rather, this is a tikkun soferim (which the Sages, of blessed memory, reversed to write thus) (Bereshit Rabbah)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:18.041146946Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}